<title>PORTUGAL: Opel resumes output in Portugal after strike.</title>
<headline>Opel resumes output in Portugal after strike.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Opel Portugal, a unit of U.S. carmaker General Motors Corp, said on Thursday it had resumed output at a Portuguese factory after a one-day stoppage caused by a strike by Spanish truck drivers.</p>
<p>&quot;The factory of Opel Portugal in Azambuja resumes normal production today,&quot; a statement said.</p>
<p>The plant had ceased production of Opel Combo and Opel Corsa vans on Wednesday because of a dire shortage of parts held up by the strike.</p>
<p>The Azambuja plant, 30 km (19 miles) north of Lisbon, normally assembles 240 vans per day.</p>
<p>Spanish truckers said on Wednesday they had called off a two-week-old strike to press for better labour conditions.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
